cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "kets-outlook: K-ETS allowance price outlook and K-MSR operating-rule model"
message: "If you use this model or its outputs, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - name: "PLANiT Institute"
    website: "https://planit.institute"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PLANiT-Institute/kets-outlook"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
abstract: >-
  A calibrated equilibrium model of the Korean Emissions Trading Scheme (K-ETS)
  that projects KAU allowance prices for 2026-2040 and evaluates operating rules
  for the Korean Market Stability Reserve (K-MSR) legislated in April 2026.
  Combines a static Coase equilibrium, a step marginal abatement cost curve built
  bottom-up from technology data, constrained Hotelling intertemporal arbitrage,
  and a liquidity transmission parameter (lambda) estimated from the observed
  price wedge. Scenario levers cover the cap path, MSR design, auction reserve
  price, hydrogen and electricity price trajectories, technology learning rates,
  and abatement capital cost. Exposed as a CLI, a web API, and an MCP server.
keywords:
  - emissions trading
  - carbon pricing
  - market stability reserve
  - Korea
  - K-ETS
  - marginal abatement cost
  - Hotelling
